{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1238546-how-do-or-would-you-use-crossover-with-existing-elements","id":1238546,"title":"How do or would you use crossover with Existing elements?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-25T04:02:23-07:00","id":1238546,"title":"How do or would you use crossover with Existing elements?","content":"Carrying on from the thoughts I had while discussing things on the 'Changing Cosmology' thread. Primary while looking at the Technocracy vs other supernaturals in crossover. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1229954-if-you-could-revise-cwod-cosmology?p=1238544#post1238544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is why you get the &quot;Vampires police their own&quot; from the departments that don't just assume it's a drug deal gone bad when they hear about a monstrous killing. Why their not kicking down the door of every Pentex subsidiary and why they are not always chasing after reports of urban 'bear' attacks. But they are VERY concerned about the people who want the Consensus to change, don't have real issues with revealing to parts of the world that Science isn't all there is. This is also why they ARE an interesting antagonist to throw into another splat's game on occasion because part of that is looking at WHY they have shown up, what part of the global conspiracy have the characters inadvertently stumbled upon or upset. Nothing needs to be altered in this case, because it rides off the back of how things are; when the Vampire coterie helped the wrong mortal, or killed the wrong person, or influenced an affair and suddenly have the MiB tracking them. Maybe the garou pack destroys a Weaver facility with a supposedly harmful product, not knowing it was a Lab (or attached to) of the Progenitors who were dealing with an issue that could wipe out that town or city so the NWO requests aid from the Void Engineers and Iteration X and suddenly the pack have HITmarks and Power Armoured umbral adversaries to deal with and again it's all par the course for what's already written rather than having to re-imagine things.<br /> <br /> OR you play a Union game and stumble across some of the Pentex stuff you'd normally only see in Werewolf and all the threads you could use from that, maybe there is internal corruption with the local Syndicate that's support this subsidiary, maybe someone has gone Malfaen Nephandi, maybe because a lot of the Pentex stuff is actually quite covert themselves and that they are killing local supernatural oppositions (Vampire AND Garou) without being obvious themselves AND that their business is good for local economy (and therefore human well being, for a given value) any side effects are being written off or let slide because there are bigger threats and issues on the plate. This even works in a Traditions game but I think is more fun when applied from a Union character PoV). Your not taking anything away or even changing anything when things are used this way.<br /> <br /> In fact the existing scope for using the tools of the different games as they stand is rather broad, the cosmologies (which is the spirit world affairs their of) fit with minimal work if any around the core games. Game mechanics are the trickier side of things but there is advice there too.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What ideas and thoughts do you have for using existing parts of one game line in another. Not looking at making sweeping changes here, but literally lifting the lore of Magadon off the page of the Book of the Wyrm and throwing it out into a Mage or Wraith game maybe. Or instead of a Baali you have a Celestial Chorus Nephandi as your coterie's adversary, or maybe your Horizon Trotting mages end up having to deal with some BSDs and the Umbral Realms closer to earth's shadow (or those presented in the Umbra books). What does the coming of Anthelios really look like (apart from the side mention of Balor's eye) if you sue it as a plot element in your Changeling game? <br /> <br /> Open forum to share cool story ideas and a bit of a mix mash up without massively altering the status quo :-) Enjoy!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}